From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office-wp14 <wp14@office.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:14:19 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] engine: number locale in Prefs, display *_in, CSV save and
 open, sheet.read, copy, paste

Session.prefs.num_locale (not saved) picks the locale of displayed and typed text. display::format_in,
cell_text_in, value_text_in, range_text_in and edit_text_in follow it (built-in ids 14 and 22 show the
locale's short date; the editor text of a number or date types back to itself); the old functions are
the en-US wrappers. A new CSV from a ru or uz session uses ; (one constant, LOCALE_CSV_LIST_SEPARATOR);
a comma-delimited file is always en-US in both directions; CsvOptions.locale reads fields as typed.
sheet.read formatted, the system clipboard text and pasted text follow the locale. Stored data does
not: xlsx parts are byte-equal across locales (test).
---
